Replaced the linear scan with a lazily built direct lookup table from message number to the first matching profile entry, so each call becomes a single array load instead of a loop. The table is built once on the first call and preserves the original first-match semantics for duplicates and NULL for unknown numbers.

```cpp
const Profile::MESG* Profile::GetMesg(const FIT_UINT16 num)
{
    static const Profile::MESG* lookup[65536] = {};
    static bool initialized = false;
    if (!initialized)
    {
        for (int i = 0; i < MESGS; i++)
        {
            if (lookup[mesgs[i].num] == NULL)
                lookup[mesgs[i].num] = &mesgs[i];
        }
        initialized = true;
    }
    return lookup[num];
}
```